<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine trade deficit widens sharply in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ukraine trade deficit widens sharply in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine's trade deficit widened sharply in 1996 to $4.14 billion, the Statistics Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>UKRAINE MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Dec 96  Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>    Exports (bln $)	     14.06	 12.57	 12.73</p>
<p>    Imports (bln $)	     18.20	 13.41	 15.44</p>
<p>    Trade balance (bln $)     -4.14	 -0.84	 -2.71</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures for trade with all countries.</p>
<p>The ministry said main export destinations in 1996 were Russia, China and Belarus. Large increase in imports in December represents seasonal imports of energy, mainly gas.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
